        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/7SZLp7kblq_-FjW4VJh3H7jVEXQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/26659_SteakTipMarinade_ddms_4x3_step2-f9f6cfc63de84d5bb0e91af3a4d0df22.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/26659/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place steaks in marinade and turn to coat. Cover and refrigerate for at least 1 hour.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/AKalC_674QoHixdYdvpy5eOcjW4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/26659_SteakTipMarinade_ddms_4x3_step3-ba569a99a420498e8edac302000a64dd.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/26659/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat an outdoor grill for high heat and lightly oil the grate. Place steaks on preheated grill; discard marinade. Cook steaks until they are beginning to firm and are hot and slightly pink in the center, about 10 minutes per side, or to desired doneness. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read 140 degrees F (60 degrees C) for medium.",
